<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Mandara Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1902 CE (approx.) · capital Mora</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Sultanate of the Wandala people at the foot of the Mandara mountains, which long held off both Bornu and the Fulani jihad.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Wandala kingdom developed on the plains north of the Mandara mountains, on the borderlands of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. It was established by the 16th century, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bornu">Bornu</a> sources mention it, and its capital moved between Keroua, Doulo and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mora-cameroon">Mora</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Mandara's ruler, the tlikse, became a Muslim sultan in the early 18th century. The kingdom worked iron from the mountains and raided the non-Muslim mountain communities for slaves. It alternated between war and alliance with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kanem-bornu-empire">Kanem-Bornu Empire</a>, and in the 19th century fought off the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/adamawa-emirate">Adamawa Emirate</a>, though it lost territory.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>German forces occupied Mandara around 1902, and it became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kamerun">German Kamerun</a> and later <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-cameroon">French Cameroon</a>, with a small portion in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. The sultan of Mandara remains a traditional ruler at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mora-cameroon">Mora</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/mandara-kingdom.jpg" alt="Mandara Kingdom" width="320" height="317"><figcaption>Image: Arrantzaleak; derivative work by rowanwindwhistler · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Borno_in_1810-es.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1902 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mora</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Wandala</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/cameroon">Cameroon</a>, <a href="/countries/nigeria">Nigeria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Wandala, Sultanate of Mandara, Mandara</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1701&amp;focus=mandara-kingdom" aria-label="Mandara Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5069 1766 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Mandara Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5389 2022L5399 1946M5389 2022L5256 2278"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5399 1946h0M5256 2278h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5389 2022h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5389 2022h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mora. <a href="/atlas?year=1701&amp;focus=mandara-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

